Quoting  Topi Linkala  <nes@iki.fi>:
>All this it seems because these things guarantee unlimited number of 
>items. Score is not the reason say many, experience nada but ulimited 
>number of items is an horror.

Unlimited items is not the problem; unlimited items with no threat is the
problem.

Yes; I would hate to see the situation you outline where you've got no
candles and no way of getting more (although with better resource
management you would always have kept an emergency wish). That doesn't
mean the answer has to be an unlimited supply of quest monsters to farm.

I'd like to see the game length potentially unlimited with no hard clock
(well, OK, _eventually_ an extinctionist will kill everything, but that's
not really within the scope of a normal game); but with a soft clock that
steadily increases difficulty if you delay.
